// Probe set for category `read` (9 atoms × 15 probes = 135 probes).
// Notes:
//   - Scorer choice rationale:
//     * exact_match_string for short canonical answers (case-insensitive, whitespace-stripped).
//     * mcq_letter for multiple-choice probes (passage_integration L1/L2/L3, distractor_filter L1).
//     * substring_all for multi-token policy-recall answers where paraphrase wording can vary.
//     * exact_match_numeric is avoided in favor of exact_match_string with a fixed format
//       instruction in the prompt, so the scorer matches on the literal string the prompt asks for.
//   - For read.cross_document_synthesis the source card says L1 ("1 doc") "does not apply".
//     I interpret L1 here as the minimal cross-document case: 2 docs, direct lookup, no
//     paraphrase, no chained reference. L2 keeps 2 docs but adds paraphrase. L3 uses 3+ docs
//     with chained reference or set operations.
//   - For read.distractor_filter L1 ("adjacent_blank") I avoid using literal HTML/UI rendering
//     and instead instantiate the distractor pattern as adjacent empty cells / blank list slots
//     in plain text — preserving the cognitive task without leaking Mind2Web wording.
//   - For read.formal_notation_parse all probes are deterministically scored by a numeric/string
//     answer; the cognitive load is parsing the notation, not symbolic computation that exceeds
//     the atom (computation is light: tabulating a finite sum or stepping a recursion).
//   - For read.event_enumeration ground truth is always a count, so the scorer is exact_match_string
//     on a single integer string.
//
// === Subagent review pass ===
// An Explore subagent critiqued this file. Applied fixes:
//   - formal_notation_parse.L3.005: ground truth corrected 91 → 98. The probe is a variant
//     of McCarthy-91 with -3 / +5 constants (instead of -10 / +11), so the canonical "91"
//     answer does NOT apply: f(99)=f(f(104))=f(101)=98.
//   - policy_recall.L3.001: replaced brittle substring_all on phrase identifiers (prone to
//     "DOB" / "last four" paraphrase failures) with a numeric-hour answer in the workflow doc.
//   - formal_notation_parse.L1.004: replaced redundant linear-function eval with an
//     indicator-function (primality) sum, to diversify L1 surface forms.
//   - distractor_filter.L1.001: replaced the form-field UI probe (Mind2Web-shaped) with a
//     planet-quiz with blank answer slots. Same atom, less benchmark-shape leakage.
//   - event_enumeration.L2.001: replaced football-field-goal probe (DROP-shaped, cf.
//     Suisham/Longwell evidence) with a personal-vs-work-emails counting probe.
//   - event_enumeration.L1.002: clarified counting convention to "individual sneezes" and
//     removed the ambiguous "sneezed twice" phrasing.
//   - event_enumeration.L3.005: changed the criterion to "two motor vehicles both moving at
//     the moment of collision" (excludes cyclists) and adjusted GT from 2 to 1; the rewritten
//     passage replaces the "delivery van clipped a cyclist" event with a rear-end at a red
//     light, eliminating the vehicle-vs-cyclist ambiguity.
//   - cross_document_synthesis.L1.005: switched scorer to order-independent substring_all on
//     the two country names so "China and Nepal" / "Nepal and China" / "Nepal,China" all pass.
//   - passage_integration.L3.001 and L3.002: added option-level annotations so all clinical
//     criteria needed to weigh the clues are passage-derivable; the atom test is the weighing,
//     not the recall of textbook medical patterns.
//
// Declined critiques (with rationale):
//   - locate_named_value.L3.001..L3.005 (the L3 probes use min/max aggregation): kept. The
//     atom card defines L3 as "implicit reference (the salaries column)"; the source
//     benchmarks instantiate this exactly via max/min/extremum queries against an
//     implicitly-named column. Removing the aggregation would collapse these to L2
//     synonym-match. The aggregation IS the implicit-reference mechanism here.
//   - passage_integration.L3.003..L3.005 (database / applicant / route vignettes): kept.
//     Each option carries a parenthetical annotation listing its key features, so the
//     criterion for weighing clues is on-passage; world knowledge is not strictly required.
//   - distractor_filter.L1.003 / L1.005 (still UI/table-row blank-slot patterns): kept.
//     The atom is sourced from Mind2Web, so the "candidate selection from adjacent items
//     including blanks" cognitive task IS the atom. The L1 set has been diversified across
//     SKU sizes, button labels, currency codes, and a planet quiz to avoid surface monoculture.
//   - policy_recall.L2 / cross_document_synthesis.L2 uniform shape: kept. The level axes
//     ("section name does not match user phrasing" / "2 docs, simple lookup-by-key with
//     paraphrase") intrinsically constrain the structure. Surface domains across the 5
//     probes are diversified (HR, travel, library, software, dormancy / music, company,
//     sports, literature, athletics).
