{"probe_id":"read.identify_query.L3.001","canonical_id":"read.identify_query","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"instruction_specificity":"buried_in_narrative"},"prompt":"My grandmother used to make cookies every Sunday afternoon. She would sit in her favorite chair by the window, humming softly. The kitchen always smelled wonderful. She had a recipe she wrote on a yellow card; it called for 2 cups of flour, 1 cup of sugar, half a stick of butter, and 1 egg. I miss those days. Anyway, I'm trying to make a triple batch tonight for a party. How many eggs will I need? --- What concrete value is the speaker asking for? Reply with exactly one of: number_of_eggs, number_of_cups_flour, number_of_sticks_butter, number_of_cups_sugar.","ground_truth":"number_of_eggs","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"number_of_eggs","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["buried_in_narrative"]}
{"probe_id":"read.identify_query.L3.002","canonical_id":"read.identify_query","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"instruction_specificity":"buried_in_narrative"},"prompt":"I've been planning a road trip from Chicago to Denver for months. My car is a 2019 Honda Civic. I love its fuel efficiency and the comfortable seats. The route I'm taking is roughly 1,000 miles. I plan to stop at a few national parks along the way and visit my old college roommate in Lincoln, Nebraska. I'm also bringing my dog, who tends to get carsick if we drive for more than 4 hours straight. With a fuel economy of 33 mpg and gas prices averaging $3.50/gallon, what should I budget for fuel for the round trip? --- What concrete value is the speaker asking for? Reply with exactly one of: fuel_budget_round_trip, total_miles, fuel_economy, hotel_budget.","ground_truth":"fuel_budget_round_trip","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"fuel_budget_round_trip","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["buried_in_narrative"]}
{"probe_id":"read.identify_query.L3.003","canonical_id":"read.identify_query","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"instruction_specificity":"buried_in_narrative"},"prompt":"Maria opened a small bakery on Maple Street five years ago. The first year was tough — she barely made rent. By year three she had hired two part-time employees. Last year revenue grew 18%, costs grew 12%, and she opened a second location. The second location uses a different supplier. Now she's debating whether to franchise. As her accountant, I noticed her overall profit margin last year. What was last year's profit margin if revenue was $480,000 and costs were $384,000? --- What single value is the speaker asking for? Reply with exactly one of: profit_margin, revenue, total_costs, growth_rate.","ground_truth":"profit_margin","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"profit_margin","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["buried_in_narrative"]}
{"probe_id":"read.identify_query.L3.004","canonical_id":"read.identify_query","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"instruction_specificity":"buried_in_narrative"},"prompt":"A new species of beetle was discovered in a rainforest in Borneo in 2018. The beetle has iridescent green wings and feeds primarily on rotting fruit. Local researchers have been monitoring its population for several years. They observed an initial population of 500 individuals. The population has been growing at roughly 8% per year. The rainforest is being threatened by logging. With these growth rates, what will the population be after 5 years? --- What concrete value is the speaker asking for? Reply with exactly one of: population_after_5_years, initial_population, growth_rate, current_year.","ground_truth":"population_after_5_years","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"population_after_5_years","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["buried_in_narrative"]}
{"probe_id":"read.identify_query.L3.005","canonical_id":"read.identify_query","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"instruction_specificity":"buried_in_narrative"},"prompt":"Email from manager: 'Hi team, hope everyone had a great weekend! As you know, our project has been making excellent progress thanks to your hard work. The client meeting last Tuesday went really well — they were very impressed. We have a few items to address, but most importantly, given that the integration tests are now stable and the design review is complete, I'd like to know whether we can ship by Friday. Please advise.' --- What single yes/no decision is the manager asking the team for? Reply with exactly one of: ship_by_friday, design_complete, tests_stable, client_satisfied.","ground_truth":"ship_by_friday","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"ship_by_friday","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["buried_in_narrative"]}
