{"probe_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis.L3.003","canonical_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_docs":"3","relation":"set_difference"},"prompt":"Doc 1: A recipe for chocolate chip cookies needs flour, sugar, butter, eggs, and chocolate chips.\nDoc 2: Pantry contents: flour, sugar, salt, baking soda.\nDoc 3: Refrigerator contents: butter, milk, eggs.\n\nQuestion: Which ingredient needed for the cookie recipe is NOT available in either the pantry or the refrigerator? Output only the missing ingredient in lowercase.","ground_truth":"chocolate chips","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"chocolate chips","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["three_docs_set_difference"]}
{"probe_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis.L3.004","canonical_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_docs":"3","relation":"chained_filter"},"prompt":"Doc A — Authors and their bestseller years:\n- Liu: 2018\n- Patel: 2020\n- Smith: 2021\n- Wong: 2019\n\nDoc B — Authors and their nationalities:\n- Liu: Chinese\n- Patel: Indian\n- Smith: American\n- Wong: Chinese\n\nDoc C — Bestseller titles by year:\n- 2018: 'The Tide'\n- 2019: 'Gold Path'\n- 2020: 'Banyan'\n- 2021: 'Outpost'\n\nQuestion: Which bestseller title was written by a Chinese author whose bestseller year is later than 2018? Output only the title in single quotes, exactly as written.","ground_truth":"'Gold Path'","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"'Gold Path'","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["three_docs_chained_filter"]}
{"probe_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis.L3.005","canonical_id":"read.cross_document_synthesis","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_docs":"3","relation":"chained"},"prompt":"Doc 1 — Conference schedule:\n- Tuesday: Workshop on AI by Dr. Mehta\n- Wednesday: Workshop on Robotics by Dr. Lee\n- Thursday: Workshop on NLP by Dr. Kim\n\nDoc 2 — Speaker affiliations:\n- Dr. Mehta: MIT\n- Dr. Lee: Stanford\n- Dr. Kim: CMU\n\nDoc 3 — University locations:\n- MIT: Cambridge, MA\n- Stanford: Stanford, CA\n- CMU: Pittsburgh, PA\n\nQuestion: In which city is the university whose representative gives the Wednesday workshop located? Output only the city name (exclude the state).","ground_truth":"Stanford","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Stanford","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["three_docs_chained"]}
