{"probe_id":"read.formal_notation_parse.L3.001","canonical_id":"read.formal_notation_parse","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"quantifier_depth":"single_fixed_index","notation_density":"moderate_piecewise_composition"},"prompt":"Define f: ℕ → ℕ piecewise:\n  f(n) = n / 2,    if n is even,\n  f(n) = 3n + 1,   if n is odd.\nLet O(n) = (n, f(n), f(f(n)), f(f(f(n))), …) be the orbit, indexed starting at 0. Compute the term at index 4 of O(7). Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"17","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"17","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["piecewise_orbit"]}
{"probe_id":"read.formal_notation_parse.L3.002","canonical_id":"read.formal_notation_parse","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"quantifier_depth":"multi_index_with_constraints","notation_density":"subscripts_and_nested_sums"},"prompt":"Let a_{i,j} for i,j ∈ {1,2,3} be defined by:\n  a_{i,j} =  1   if i = j,\n  a_{i,j} = −1   if i + j = 4 and i ≠ j,\n  a_{i,j} =  0   otherwise.\nCompute Σ_{i=1}^{3} Σ_{j=1}^{3} a_{i,j}. Output only the integer (use a leading '-' for negative values).","ground_truth":"1","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"1","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["piecewise_double_sum"]}
{"probe_id":"read.formal_notation_parse.L3.003","canonical_id":"read.formal_notation_parse","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"quantifier_depth":"multi_index_with_constraints","notation_density":"heavy_with_subscripts_and_overlines"},"prompt":"For integers 1 ≤ i < j ≤ 4, define x_{i,j} = 2i + j. For each j ∈ {2,3,4}, define x̄_j = Σ_{i=1}^{j−1} x_{i,j}. Compute x̄_2 + x̄_3 + x̄_4. Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"40","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":40,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["multi_index","formal_notation"],"notes":"x̄_2=4, x̄_3=12, x̄_4=24; total 40."}
{"probe_id":"read.formal_notation_parse.L3.004","canonical_id":"read.formal_notation_parse","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"quantifier_depth":"multi_index_with_constraints","notation_density":"heavy_with_subscripts_and_overlines"},"prompt":"Define M_{i,j} for i,j ∈ {1,2,3,4} by:\n  M_{i,j} = i   if j > i,\n  M_{i,j} = j   if j < i,\n  M_{i,j} = 0   if i = j.\nCompute Σ_{i=1}^{4} Σ_{j=1}^{4} M_{i,j}. Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"20","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"20","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["piecewise_matrix_sum"]}
{"probe_id":"read.formal_notation_parse.L3.005","canonical_id":"read.formal_notation_parse","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"quantifier_depth":"nested_recursion","notation_density":"moderate_piecewise_recursion"},"prompt":"Define f: ℤ → ℤ piecewise:\n  f(n) = n − 3,           if n > 100,\n  f(n) = f(f(n + 5)),     if n ≤ 100.\nCompute f(99). Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"98","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"98","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["nested_recursion"],"notes":"f(99)=f(f(104))=f(101)=98. Author note: variant of McCarthy-91 with constants -3/+5 (instead of -10/+11), so the answer is NOT 91."}
