{"probe_id":"read.event_enumeration.L3.001","canonical_id":"read.event_enumeration","category":"read","level":"L3","axis_values":{"n_events_present":"2-3","event_specificity":"definite_description"},"prompt":"Passage: 'On the climb, Sara reached what looked like the top of the ridge but turned out not to be the real summit. Then a steep ridge brought them to another apparent peak that fooled the team into thinking they had finally succeeded. After another hour they finally crested the actual summit. Earlier, the team had paused at a small flat shoulder that nobody mistook for the top.' How many false summits are described? Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"2","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"2","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["paraphrase_event"]}
